logs/
orchestrator/.venv/
orchestrator/Caddyfile
orchestrator/caddy.log
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.claude/*
# Absorbed third-party code must carry its receipt: `equip`'s registry and audit
# reports record which upstream a skill came from, at which exact commit, and why
# anything was rejected. Ignoring them leaves reviewers with vendored code and no
# provenance. Uses `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/` because git cannot re-include
# a path whose parent directory is excluded. The nested
# `.claude/equipment/.gitignore` still keeps the clone cache out.
!.claude/equipment/
# This repository's own pre-commit gate — the four drift checks, ~1s. It is
# tracked because it IS the gate: ignored, it would exist only on the machine
# that wrote it, which is the same "it works here" failure the fleet audit found
# on four other boxes. checks.sh runs it when the repo being committed to has it,
# so it reaches every contributor through `committer` and stays out of the 40+
# unrelated repositories committer.sh also serves.
!.claude/pre-commit.sh
orchestrator/.claude/

# Build artifacts
mcp-package/dist/
mcp-package/*.egg-info/
mcp-package/build/

# Type checker cache
.mypy_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
